    "body": "<!-- pr-reviewer: e27c97a630b73e4c79430bf95c3927d0bba09207 -->\n**Ready for the maintainer to merge.**\n\nWhat looks good\n- Removing the global panic hook and catching only panics that escape `run` (`crates/ui/src/main.rs`) fixes the false box for handled panics; payload-to-text never panics (`panic_text.rs:9-17`).\n- A failed CONOUT$ open now counts as no console (`win_console.rs:96-99`).\n- No new dependency, no unwrap/expect, provenance lines present, small files, body has `Changelog:` and `Fixes`.\n\nLocal results (merged with main, built on Windows, so the Windows block in `main.rs` and `win_console.rs` was compiled)\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --bin camcraft-ui payload_text`: 1 passed\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean\n- No profile sets `panic = \"abort\"`, so `catch_unwind` works.\n\nRequested before merge: none.\n\nNotes (not blocking)\n- The box and console behaviour itself is not testable headlessly; the hand-checks listed in the PR body (double-click, terminal, redirect, forced failure) still stand for a maintainer on Windows.\n- A panic on a non-main thread that is not joined into `run` will no longer show a box; that appears intended.\n\nA maintainer will approve and merge by hand.\n",
